{"term": "Schlampe", "lang": "de", "script": "latin", "romanization": null, "category": "insults", "subcategory": "slut_shame", "concept": "slut_shame", "is_novel_concept": false, "register": "slang_crude", "crude": 85, "technical": 0, "recognition_pct_current": 98, "recognition_pct_peak": 98, "peak_year": null, "regional": null, "definition": "Slut or bitch; the primary German slur for a sexually promiscuous or slovenly woman; also used as a general female-directed insult equivalent to 'bitch'.", "english_term": "slut", "english_translation_quality": "approximate", "notes": "Covers both 'slut' (sexual promiscuity) and 'bitch' (general female contempt) in German; semantic range is broader than either single English term; among the most common female-directed insults in the language."}
