{"term": "Saukerl", "lang": "de", "script": "latin", "romanization": null, "category": "insults", "subcategory": "filth_insult", "concept": "bastard_insult", "is_novel_concept": false, "register": "slang_crude", "crude": 55, "technical": 0, "recognition_pct_current": 85, "recognition_pct_peak": 85, "peak_year": null, "regional": null, "definition": "Pig fellow; Sau (sow) + Kerl (fellow/man); a mild-to-moderate insult for an unpleasant, slovenly, or disagreeable man; slightly folksy in register.", "english_term": "dirty dog", "english_translation_quality": "approximate", "notes": "Milder than Schweinhund in most contemporary usage; Sau invokes piggishness (filth, greed, sloth) rather than any specific sexual act; used affectionately in some regional dialects among friends."}
