{"term": "Muterficker", "lang": "de", "script": "latin", "romanization": null, "category": "insults", "subcategory": "maternal_insult", "concept": "motherfucker_insult", "is_novel_concept": false, "register": "slang_crude", "crude": 95, "technical": 0, "recognition_pct_current": 88, "recognition_pct_peak": 90, "peak_year": null, "regional": null, "definition": "Motherfucker; Mutter (mother) + Ficker (fucker); German calque of the English expletive; among the strongest insults in contemporary German.", "english_term": "motherfucker", "english_translation_quality": "direct", "notes": "Standard orthography is Mutterficker (double t); this form has one t, possibly a phonetic variant, corpus artifact, or non-standard regional spelling; popularized substantially through American media dubbing and hip-hop influence."}
